    {
      "seed": 1494397186,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "id": "ITYM-sjOvWIZxqmYjcvgi",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "roughness": 0,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "fontSize": 28,
      "opacity": 100,
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "updated": 1776725418333,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "THis dependens on batch.size and linger.ms\nIn most cases, GZIP and ZStd provide the best compression ratios, \nat a slightly higher CPU cost, while Snappy and\n LZ4 tend to reduce CPU cost at the expense of lower compression ratios. \nHowever, the actual result is very dependent on the actual type of load.\n\n",
      "version": 828,
      "autoResize": true,
      "type": "text",
