    },
    {
      "isDeleted": false,
      "locked": false,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "link": null,
      "roughness": 1,
      "groupIds": [
        "967x5Gta9mX6jxn_Wknff"
      ],
      "index": "bI8",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "angle": 0,
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "version": 1096,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "type": "rectangle",
      "updated": 1776725451679,
      "id": "N47Q5bg1b7zmbZhs09tj-",
      "x": 3463.646150782104,
      "seed": 149914078,
      "boundElements": [],
      "y": 122.98267587311,
      "opacity": 100,
      "height": 361.12547204574116,
      "width": 858.836536175645,
      "frameId": null,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "versionNonce": 1952253240
    },
    {
      "seed": 1771306270,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "id": "0PU8WnebGymO2RrrIAQBj",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "roughness": 0,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "fontSize": 28,
      "opacity": 100,
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "updated": 1776725451679,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Deserialization ( key.deserializer, value.deserializer # note: broker only know raw bytes)\n2. poll and process\n      Fetching != polling ( consumer fetches and caches on consumer)\n      poll get data from cache & hence the count.\n         - max.poll.records #default 500\n         - poll() loop provides a proxy for : check if consumer is alive, session timeouts, heartbeats\n         - max.poll.internal.ms : to check above there is a time limit: \n            # if exceeds then trigger  session timeout, the consumer group coordinator will revoke its \n               partition assignment\n3. commit record offsets\n         - enable.auto.commit = true, depends on auto.commit.interval.ms : #default  5 seconds\n           # above is default or auto commit based on number of records polled in poll() api call\n         - maual comit: explicity calll conumer.commit()  and enable.auto.commit to false\n       ",
      "version": 1431,
      "autoResize": true,
      "type": "text",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "index": "bIY",
      "roundness": null,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Deserialization ( key.deserializer, value.deserializer # note: broker only know raw bytes)\n2. poll and process\n      Fetching != polling ( consumer fetches and caches on consumer)\n      poll get data from cache & hence the count.\n         - max.poll.records #default 500\n         - poll() loop provides a proxy for : check if consumer is alive, session timeouts, heartbeats\n         - max.poll.internal.ms : to check above there is a time limit: \n            # if exceeds then trigger  session timeout, the consumer group coordinator will revoke its \n               partition assignment\n3. commit record offsets\n         - enable.auto.commit = true, depends on auto.commit.interval.ms : #default  5 seconds\n           # above is default or auto commit based on number of records polled in poll() api call\n         - maual comit: explicity calll conumer.commit()  and enable.auto.commit to false\n       ",
      "height": 490,
      "link": null,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "groupIds": [],
      "versionNonce": 771202616,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "frameId": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "x": 4554.9570379685465,
      "angle": 0,
      "y": 435.64968785782776,
      "width": 1379.4193115234375
    },
    {
      "seed": 494312158,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "id": "__0px7Jd3UPIQY2hhSnlj",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "roughness": 0,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "fontSize": 28,
      "opacity": 100,
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "updated": 1776725451679,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Key points:\n    - only fetch.min.bytes : is important the min bytes to returs ( or satified)\n    -      fetch.max.bytes : no hard limit, \n                 # Data is written to .log as a single serialization (batch of records), the IO threads\n                    will not break up in chunk or it will not deserialize message. So if the requested data exists\n                    even if blob is larger than fetch.max.bytes the broker will return the blob.\n    -      max.partition.fetch.bytes: same max logic applies to partiction fetch bytes\n    -      fetch.max.wait.ms:  purgatory : once fetch.min.bytes or this param is reaches, response object is constructed\n            \n ",
      "version": 1042,
      "autoResize": true,
      "type": "text",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "index": "bIc",
      "roundness": null,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Key points:\n    - only fetch.min.bytes : is important the min bytes to returs ( or satified)\n    -      fetch.max.bytes : no hard limit, \n                 # Data is written to .log as a single serialization (batch of records), the IO threads\n                    will not break up in chunk or it will not deserialize message. So if the requested data exists\n                    even if blob is larger than fetch.max.bytes the broker will return the blob.\n    -      max.partition.fetch.bytes: same max logic applies to partiction fetch bytes\n    -      fetch.max.wait.ms:  purgatory : once fetch.min.bytes or this param is reaches, response object is constructed\n            \n ",
      "height": 350,
      "link": null,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "groupIds": [],
      "versionNonce": 1792481080,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "frameId": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "x": 4570.838776033896,
      "angle": 0,
      "y": 117.27868962996945,
      "width": 1611.8192138671875
    },
    {
      "seed": 237518402,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "id": "OEB5m2fhnR20mFhGzlwKE",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "roughness": 0,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "fontSize": 28,
      "opacity": 100,
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "updated": 1776725451679,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "group.id:\nconsumer.subscribe(topic) or if you want to make use of kafka's built-in\n    offset management ( you need to set group.id)\npartition.assignment.strategy:\n    - RangeAssignor : # think about stream join based on key\n    - RoundRobinAssignor:\n    - Sticky Assignor : # important when consumer leaves a group.\n          unaffected partition doesnt leave group.\n    - CooperativeStickyAssignor: # incremental rebalanceing and eventual\nauto.offset.reset: # where to read from if no valid offset is found\n\nMetrics:  assigned-partions, rebalance-latency-avg, rebalance-total, \n           consumer-lag-offsets",
      "version": 887,
      "autoResize": true,
      "type": "text",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "index": "bId",
      "roundness": null,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "group.id:\nconsumer.subscribe(topic) or if you want to make use of kafka's built-in\n    offset management ( you need to set group.id)\npartition.assignment.strategy:\n    - RangeAssignor : # think about stream join based on key\n    - RoundRobinAssignor:\n    - Sticky Assignor : # important when consumer leaves a group.\n          unaffected partition doesnt leave group.\n    - CooperativeStickyAssignor: # incremental rebalanceing and eventual\nauto.offset.reset: # where to read from if no valid offset is found\n\nMetrics:  assigned-partions, rebalance-latency-avg, rebalance-total, \n           consumer-lag-offsets",
      "height": 455,
      "link": null,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "groupIds": [],
      "versionNonce": 794783800,
