    {
      "seed": 1115565128,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "id": "EHWZzqkeD8eLFZuy3eYzt",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "roughness": 1,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "opacity": 100,
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "updated": 1776725437473,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "How to set - Trial at 0, 512, 1048576 and then iterate based on the throughput\nand end-to-end latency achieved at each level",
      "version": 585,
      "autoResize": false,
      "type": "text",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "index": "bmC",
      "roundness": null,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "How to set - Trial at 0, 512, 1048576 and then iterate based on the throughput and end-to-end latency achieved at each level",
      "height": 50,
      "link": null,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "groupIds": [
        "Xufv_bOU0joIzcTv4DzpR"
      ],
      "versionNonce": 469331272,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "frameId": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "x": -19.781661618823364,
      "angle": 0,
      "y": 7769.3772184080535,
      "width": 795.1595458984375
    },
    {
      "seed": 964780872,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "id": "P95933kzHp1yAEnmlsD4z",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "roughness": 1,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "opacity": 100,
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "updated": 1776725437473,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Explanation - By setting this value above 0 you can force the fetcher thread to\nwait more time (up to replica.fetch.wait.max.ms) before it completes the fetch\nrequest. Less fetch requests mean less load on the cluster which improves\nthroughput and end-to-end latency. This may increase the end-to-end latency for\nsome of the records but the improved performance may lead to better end-to-\nend latency all round.",
      "version": 584,
      "autoResize": false,
      "type": "text",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "index": "bmD",
      "roundness": null,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Explanation - By setting this value above 0 you can force the fetcher thread to wait more time (up to replica.fetch.wait.max.ms) before it completes the fetch request. Less fetch requests mean less load on the cluster which improves throughput and end-to-end latency. This may increase the end-to-end latency for some of the records but the improved performance may lead to better end-to-end latency all round.",
      "height": 150,
      "link": null,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "groupIds": [
        "Xufv_bOU0joIzcTv4DzpR"
      ],
      "versionNonce": 602702920,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
