      "y": -1068.7792838757377,
      "opacity": 100,
      "height": 657.4051610270562,
      "width": 1014.8939087730442,
      "frameId": null,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "versionNonce": 1756895544
    },
    {
      "seed": 1300234056,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "id": "eLJfln5weo_3hwG4O7AMe",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "roughness": 0,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "fontSize": 28,
      "opacity": 100,
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "updated": 1776725418333,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "For Kafka clients, io-ratio and io-wait-ratio let you see if the bottleneck\nis the client, the brokers, or the network.\n\nio-ratio ≈ fraction of time the client thread is doing network I/O\n(sending requests / reading responses). \nio-wait-ratio ≈ fraction of time the client thread is idle, waiting for I/O\n(no work to do, waiting on broker responses / data). \n**Client processing fraction** (your app code + client-side processing) is:\nclient_processing_ratio = 1 - io-ratio - io-wait-ratio\n\nHow to read them:\n\nIf 1 - io-ratio - io-wait-ratio ≈ 1 → most time is in client processing ⇒\nyour app/client logic is the bottleneck.\nIf io-ratio ≈ 1 → client is busy doing I/O almost all the time ⇒ heavy\nnetwork/disk I/O; brokers and/or network are likely being driven hard.\nIf io-wait-ratio ≈ 1 → client is mostly idle, just waiting ⇒ brokers (or\nupstream/downstream system) are likely the bottleneck, not the client.",
      "version": 422,
      "autoResize": true,
      "type": "text",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "index": "bts",
      "roundness": null,
      "containerId": "gJL3Bsgnj0Qu8QqEHqYdH",
      "originalText": "For Kafka clients, io-ratio and io-wait-ratio let you see if the bottleneck is the client, the brokers, or the network.\n\nio-ratio ≈ fraction of time the client thread is doing network I/O (sending requests / reading responses). \nio-wait-ratio ≈ fraction of time the client thread is idle, waiting for I/O (no work to do, waiting on broker responses / data). \n**Client processing fraction** (your app code + client-side processing) is:\nclient_processing_ratio = 1 - io-ratio - io-wait-ratio\n\nHow to read them:\n\nIf 1 - io-ratio - io-wait-ratio ≈ 1 → most time is in client processing ⇒ your app/client logic is the bottleneck.\nIf io-ratio ≈ 1 → client is busy doing I/O almost all the time ⇒ heavy network/disk I/O; brokers and/or network are likely being driven hard.\nIf io-wait-ratio ≈ 1 → client is mostly idle, just waiting ⇒ brokers (or upstream/downstream system) are likely the bottleneck, not the client.",
      "height": 630,
      "link": null,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "groupIds": [
        "0trd9kOHpenL0K0y3xiuU"
      ],
      "versionNonce": 231748152,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "frameId": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "x": -4328.561701684312,
      "angle": 0,
      "y": -1063.7792838757377,
      "width": 998.53564453125
    },
    {
      "isDeleted": false,
      "locked": false,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "link": null,
      "roughness": 0,
      "groupIds": [],
      "index": "btt",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "angle": 0,
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "version": 267,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "type": "rectangle",
